WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.370
-You mentioned your son.
He is graduating from 1st grade?

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:04.070 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-1st grade tomorrow.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's his little
graduation ceremony.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What is a
graduation ceremony --

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.076
What are you expecting from
a 1st-grade graduation ceremony?

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I believe they will say,
"You are all now 2nd graders."

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:19.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And all of us will be crying
and saying, "Yes!

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:21.421 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You did it!"

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, what is your son into
as a 7-year-old?

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, recently,
my son was on a playdate,

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very unusual playdate,
I thought.

00:00:28.595 --> 00:00:30.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wasn't at the playdate,
'cause it was at the other --

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:33.500
They do this thing at my son's
school that he really loves.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're going to
someone else's house,

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can sign your child out,
and they go home with

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.338 line:92%
the other nanny or parent,

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
which makes them feel
very independent.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so he loves that.
-Of course.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:44.144
-So, I had signed him out
to go to this playdate

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.547
with a few girlfriends that he's
very close with in his class.

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
And during the playdate, I
had received a video.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:53.186
And the mom said,
"Oh, they're having so much fun.

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:56.256
They're doing a
little fashion show right now."

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.357 line:92%
So, she sent me the video.

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.959 size:78% position:39%
And the two girls in
the playdate come out

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
looking like
beautiful princesses.

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my son
comes out wearing

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.533 line:92%
a full princess dress, as well.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:11.237
He used purple marker
to make eye shadow and contour.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:17.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he gave his best walk
and then he went, "Fashion!"

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:21.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I said,
"Where did you learn this?

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, what was
your inspiration for this?"

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:28.988
And he said, "Oh, it's because
I watched 'RuPaul's Drag Race.'"

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.124 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:33.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-It's amazing.

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:33.760 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And for a moment,
I questioned my parenting,

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.263 size:78% position:39% line:92%
but then I said, "No.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is amazing that,
first of all,

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.767 line:92%
he picked up some good tips."

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:41.401 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes. Exactly.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:42.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Second, I'm
proud that my son knows

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:45.638 size:84% position:42%
"RuPaul's Drag Race"
and can, like, compete.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, he could
have flipped over a table,

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:48.908 line:92%
like the New Jersey Housewives.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
I might have been a
little more embarrassed

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:51.377 line:92%
if he watched that with me.

00:01:51.377 --> 00:01:53.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly. There's some
decency to the way

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
they go about themselves
in "Drag Race," yeah.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:59.052
So, congratulations on the
final season of "Kimmy Schmidt."

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is, obviously,
your second show

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you've worked with
Tina Fey and Robert Carlock.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:06.726
Is it true that Tina and the
writing staff will sometimes

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
write things with
no expectations that you,

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an actor,
will actually have to do them?

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.800
-Well, first, let me say it's
gonna be very, very bittersweet

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.469
for this show to end, because
my relationship with Tina Fey

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:19.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
is my most successful and
longest-lasting relationship

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.640 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in my life.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.374 line:92%
-I mean, it's incredible.

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:23.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two shows and
two great characters.

00:02:23.143 --> 00:02:24.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm going to
miss it terribly,

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:26.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
and especially the wacky group
of players that we have,

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Titus and Ellie
and Carol Kane.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:29.649 size:81% position:41% line:92%
We are all very close,

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:32.952
and I'm going to miss the sort
of wacky fun that we have there.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.254 line:92%
But I have noticed, sometimes,

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.288 line:92%
they put things in the script

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:38.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, because I take their
writing so seriously,

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.760
I just think is -- I'm expected
to do whatever they put there.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:44.364
And there was an episode of
"30 Rock" where they wrote --

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:47.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were fighting over the
same guy, Liz Lemon and Jenna.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was supposed to be
like that movie thing

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:51.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you go "ahh"
and then put your arm around

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:54.240 line:92%
your date, your supposed date.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, they said,
"Well, Liz does it,

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:59.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
but then Jenna does it
with her leg."

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:02.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, we did the rehearsal,
and I did that.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I was like --
I can't do it here, 'cause...

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
-...you'll be off the air.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:11.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I literally did it,
and she was like,

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We never expected that
you could do that."

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just wrote that as, like,
an imagery, like an idea.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:20.066 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was like, "Oh, I thought --
Like, I practiced at home."

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:25.471
-Exactly. You're like,
"I was the Dining Car, Ms. Fey!"

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:28.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here, Jane.

